#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Conway's 99-Graph Problem — Class 6 (Single-Cycle 12-Vertex Seed) GPU Trie Solver (Gen V.6g)
============================================================================================
Unified standalone C++/CUDA 4-Level Prefix Trie Solver covering all 2,670 / 2,670 Class 6
canonical B6-orbits partitioned into 207 bundles:
  - Bundles   0..163 (IDs 20000..20170): 164 Remaining Saddle-Free Super-Bundles across Shards 0..5
                                         (covering all 2,400 remaining uncertified Class 6 orbits)
  - Bundles 164..206 (IDs 10000..10042): 43 Certified UNSAT Bundles
                                         (covering all 270 certified UNSAT Class 6 orbits)

Gen V.6g Architecture (Benchmarked on NVIDIA A100-SXM4-40GB: 59.85s on Bundle 20008 Batch 145/363,
4.73x faster than Gen V.4, 192 B stack frame, 35,400 B shared memory, 4 blocks/SM = 55,296 threads):
  - Macro Constants + Const Struct References (68.8% stack frame reduction: 616 B -> 192 B)
  - Shared-Memory Hoisted s_x7_2[128] + Stage C Symmetric Reverse-Sandwich (x9 -> x8)
  - Law M13 Zero-Truncation Overflow Guard (ovf_code != 0 aborts immediately)
  - Per-batch deterministic checkpointing (JSON_BATCH_CKPT) + atomic bundle certificate output

Usage Examples:
  1. Run a specific bundle by ID (e.g. Bundle 20008 or Bundle 20165):
     BUNDLE_ID=20165 python3 run_class6_trie_v6_solver.py
  2. Run a specific shard (SHARD_ID=0..5) for N batches (resuming automatically from checkpoints):
     SHARD_ID=0 MAX_BATCHES=20 python3 run_class6_trie_v6_solver.py
  3. Spot-check a single batch (e.g. Batch 145 of Bundle 20008):
     BUNDLE_ID=20008 START_BATCH=145 MAX_BATCHES=1 python3 run_class6_trie_v6_solver.py
  4. Re-verify a certified bundle (e.g. Certified Bundle 10042 = Seed III Orbit 2118):
     BUNDLE_ID=10042 FORCE_RERUN=1 python3 run_class6_trie_v6_solver.py
"""
